    "https://wku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206487": {
      "title": "Associate Provost for Faculty and Academic Excellence (Internal Search)",
      "description": "Western Kentucky University\nJob Posting: Associate Provost for Faculty and Academic Excellence (Internal Search) Western Kentucky University \n\tJob Posting: Associate Provost for Faculty and Academic Excellence (Internal Search) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Provost for Faculty and Academic Excellence (Internal Search) Category: Featured Jobs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Provost/VP Academic Affairs Locations: Bowling Green, KY Posted: Nov 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 995398 Position ID: 206487 Share About Western Kentucky University: Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience and to elevating its surrounding communities. Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293 students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors, and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville, KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents. Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . Job Description: Internal Search: only WKU employees currently working in a non-temporary status are eligible to apply. The Provost invites applications and nominations for an internal search for an Associate Provost for Faculty and Academic Excellence position. Reporting to the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Associate Provost is a senior academic leader who advances faculty success, supports academic quality and effectiveness, and helps carry out the University's strategic priorities in partnership with the academic deans, academic program coordinators, department chairs, Academic Affairs Executive Team, Office of the Provost Staff, direct reports and other university stakeholders. The primary duties of the Associate Provost for Faculty and Academic Excellence are: Works collaboratively with deans to implement strategic plan initiatives. On behalf of the Provost, serves as primary liaison for faculty and administrators to resolve conflicts, complaints, and other Academic Affairs personnel related matters. Oversees logistics associated with continuance, tenure and promotion, and faculty evaluation processes. On behalf of the Provost, reviews appointment letters and oversees faculty hiring. On behalf of the Provost, works collaboratively with various Faculty Senate committees (e.g. Faculty Handbook, Academic Quality, Faculty Welfare & Professional Responsibilities, etc.). Communicates with and assembles the Advisory Committee on Faculty Continuance, Promotion and Tenure in accordance with the Faculty Handbook and serves ex-officio member. Communicates with and assembles the Advisory Committee on Faculty Grievance in accordance with the Faculty Handbook and serves as ex-officio member. Communicates with and assembles the University Complaint Committee for student grade appeals and serves as ex-officio member. In collaboration with the Provost, oversees all university-level faculty recognition and honorary degree processes. In collaboration with the Provost, oversees all university-level New Faculty Orientation and academic administrators' professional development opportunities, including new chair/director and new dean training. Supervises five direct reports including: Director of Student Publications, Director of Regional Campuses, Director of the Mahurin Honors College, Program Manager of Dual Credit, and Director of the Center for Innovative Teaching and Learning. Serves on the Academic Affairs Executive Team and works collaboratively with all members of the Office of the Provost Staff. Serves as an advisory member to the Council of Academic Deans. Either accompanies or represents the Provost at the Council of Chief Academic Officers (CCAO) meetings and events, the Board of Regents meetings and events, and other meetings and events as requested. Liaison for Campus Partners/Students of Concern. All other duties as assigned. Appointment and terms This position is a 12-month administrative appointment with a faculty tenure home in the candidate's academic department. Start date, salary and any stipend or return-to-faculty terms are negotiable. Requirements: Earned doctorate or terminal degree in an academic discipline. Rank of tenured associate or full professor, or qualifications for tenure at WKU. Demonstrated record of teaching, scholarship or creative activity, and service. Experience in academic leadership, such as department head, associate dean, program director or equivalent. Experience handling faculty personnel matters with fairness and discretion. Experience with faculty governance, shared governance structures, or collective communication with faculty bodies. Effective communication, mediation, and consensus-building skills. Additional Information: Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Application Instructions: The following items must be submitted through this electronic talent management system with review of applications beginning November 20th, although expressions of interest may be considered until the position is filled: Letter of Intent Curriculum Vita Statement of Leadership Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Names and contact information of three reference providers will be collected during the application process. Reference letters will be requested by the Search Committee through an online process at a later date. You will receive email confirmation once you have successfully completed the application process. URL: www.wku.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101"
    },
    "https://wku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206562": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Operations & Outreach (SCCJS and Political Science)",
      "description": "Western Kentucky University\nJob Posting: Coordinator, Operations & Outreach (SCCJS and Political Science) Western Kentucky University \n\tJob Posting: Coordinator, Operations & Outreach (SCCJS and Political Science) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Coordinator, Operations & Outreach (SCCJS and Political Science) Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Department of Society, Culture, Crime, & Justice Studies Locations: Bowling Green, KY Posted: Nov 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 997686 Position ID: 206562 Share About Western Kentucky University: Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience and to elevating its surrounding communities. Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293 students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors, and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville, KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents. Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . Job Description: The Potter College of Arts & Letters is accepting applications for an Operations & Outreach Coordinator to support the Society, Culture, Crime, and Justice Studies and Political Science Departments and will continue in that role within the newly formed School of Social Sciences beginning July 1, 2027. This position will work closely with academic leadership and faculty to coordinate day-to-day operations. This role requires initiative, attention to detail, and sound judgment in managing a range of administrative responsibilities. Duties include: Assist with coordination for recruiting, retention, and outreach events. Assist with coordination of marketing and promotional activities for academic programs. Schedule departmental tours for potential students. Oversee Faculty Load and Compensation process to ensure timely and accurate payment to all full-time and part-time faculty. Prepare departmental course scheduling in Banner. Support Graduate Assistantships by ensuring departmental budget accuracy, assisting with graduate assistantship forms, creating EPAFs and managing the onboarding process. Support the management of building, including classrooms, offices, common areas, and assisting on facilities projects. Ensure proper function of office and classroom equipment. Provide administrative support to department chairs and complete other special projects as needed. Communicate clearly and professionally both internally and externally from departments. Cross-train duties to provide departmental and college support when necessary. Supervise student workers to include hiring, onboarding, scheduling, approving timesheets and overseeing duties. Update departmental website and social media with new events and information. Other duties as assigned. Requirements: Bachelor's degree Additional Information: Hourly Rate:  $19.49 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Application Instructions: The following items must be submitted through this electronic talent management system. Expressions of interest may be considered until the position is filled: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcripts or Copy of Official Transcripts Names and contact information of three reference providers will be collected during the application process. Reference letters will be requested by the Search Committee through an online process at a later date. You will receive email confirmation once you have successfully completed the application process. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101"
