    "https://wku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206622": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Green River Regional Educational Cooperative",
      "description": "Western Kentucky University\nJob Posting: Executive Director, Green River Regional Educational Cooperative Western Kentucky University \n\tJob Posting: Executive Director, Green River Regional Educational Cooperative Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Executive Director, Green River Regional Educational Cooperative Category: Administrative Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Dean College of Education Locations: Bowling Green, KY Posted: Nov 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 206622 Share About Western Kentucky University: Disclaimer: The Green River Regional Educational Cooperative is an independent 501c3 non-profit Offering leadership, service, and support for high quality teaching and learning in the Green River Regional Area. Our vision is to provide services through professional networks and jointly designed solutions focused on transformational teaching, learning, and leading. Our mission is to maintain an unwavering commitment to the service and support of our schools by building adult capacities and channeling resources which increase student success in school and in life. WKU is host to the application platform supporting an independent search for the Chief Executive Officer of GRREC. Accessibility to applicant materials is reserved to the GRREC Board of Directors - Personnel Committee (BOD-PC). The BOD-PC is chaired by Superintendent Gary Fields. WKU is a partner with GRREC but is not responsible for any aspects of the search process beyond the application platform. All inquiries should be addressed to gary.fields@bgreen.kyschools.us. Job Description: The position of Chief Executive Officer for the Green River Regional Educational Cooperative is designed to be responsible for the efficient management of the Cooperative. The Board expects the CEO to administer carefully the organization and administration of both material and personnel resources in such a way as to achieve the Board's objective of the best possible programs. As the Chief Executive Officer of the Board, the CEO is the administrative head of all programs of the Cooperative. The CEO may delegate duty and authority for the operation of the various programs but retains responsibility to the Board for the results produced. It is the responsibility of the Board to attract and retain the services of a qualified and experienced educator to serve in the capacity. The CEO must have demonstrated competence and ability as an educational leader. Responsibilities: Serve as the Chief Executive Officer of GRREC. Serve as Treasurer of the Board. Administer all GRREC programs and provide supervision over GRREC activities and operations. Prepare in conjunction with the Chairman of the Board, the agenda for each Board meeting and organize monthly meetings of the Board. the preparation of minutes and proceedings of the board. Develop surveys, summaries and reports as authorized and/or requested by the Board. Maintain GRREC records. Employ staff for positions authorized by the Board of Directors. Supervise day-to-day activities and annual evaluations of staff. Plan and implement instructional support and professional development services that help support identified needs of member districts. Design and implement unified purchasing for member districts. Plan and write programs for approval and implement Instructional Leadership Training Programs for administrators. Provide for the oversight and administration of grants received for various Cooperative initiatives. Serve as liaison between Western Kentucky University's College of Education and member districts. Meet regularly with and maintain records for committees appointed by the Board. Plan and implement an annual Summer Conference for member district administrators. Meet regularly with various administrative groups from member districts to recognize and respond to emerging needs and to provide networking opportunities. Serve as the Cooperative' s liaison with the Kentucky Department of Education. Represent the Board and school districts through inter-agency collaboration and attendance at regional, state and national conferences and meetings. Inspire and lead a highly competitive organization with a governing board and Executive committee organizational structure. Identify areas of program development, implementation and growth opportunities. Systematically considers new and better ways of doing things. Adapts leadership behavior to the needs of the current situation. Demonstrates the ability to foster a healthy organizational culture, to encourage teamwork and collaboration; strong interpersonal skills that include the ability to inspire and motivate; effective at conflict management. Directs research and related projects, prepares reports, and publishes the results on subjects deemed of importance to the membership. Develops education programs to advance the professional/technical/managerial skills of the membership. Directs, plans, and executes all communications to the general membership. Maintains visibility and accessibility to membership to the greatest degree possible. Demonstrates effective use of skills and knowledge in budget preparation, allocation of resources, cost effectiveness, and financial reporting. Demonstrates knowledge of current research and theory on effective education services. Create a climate which encourages a positive working relationship among members. Show enthusiasm and initiative in the performance of administrative responsibilities. Deal with difficult and unpleasant situations with courage, objectivity, and candor. Demonstrate an ability to provide leadership and shoulder responsibility. Demonstrate good organizational skills. Be highly motivated, a self-starter, and expend the effort necessary to carry out the responsibilities of the position. Have flexibility, self-confidence, creativity, a sense of humor, and patience. Demonstrates the ability to make decisions promptly in accordance with basic goals of the organization. Perform other duties as assigned by the Board of Directors. Requirements: Certification for Superintendent, other Administrator Certification or Supervisor of Instruction Certification Minimum10 years of experience in education strongly preferred; co-op, district-level, and/or superintendent experience preferred Demonstrate competence and ability as an educational leader Project management and data-based decision-making skills; ability to promote consensus and to serve as a model for jointly designing next steps Ability to understand current and developing movements or trends for instructional improvement Utilize varied culture-driven, research-based approaches for school/district development Strong relationship, team-based management, capacity-building skills are required Excellent analytical skills; experience with data collection Strong organizational and time management skills Strong oral and written communication skills Good computer skills with a variety of programs and software, specifically the ability to create word processing and desktop publishing documents, spreadsheets and databases Ability to work independently with little direction Ability to collaborate and interface with state agencies and universities Good interpersonal skills; ability to be a team player and to promote positive public relations on behalf of the project and the organizations involved and on behalf of GRREC Additional Information: Annual Contract : 240 Days per board approved contract; Compensation for accumulated sick leave may be available after 5 years of continuous service. Reports To : Board Members Salary : Set by Board of Directors - Minimum starting salary of $165,000 which is currently the GRREC Superintendent Average Evaluations : Performed annually by the Board Application Instructions: The following items must be submitted through this electronic talent management system: Letter of Interest Resume 3 Letters of Recommendation Interested parties with questions may contact Mr. Gary Fields, Chair of the GRREC Personnel Committee: gary.fields@bgreen.kyschools.us Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101"
    },
    "https://wku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206630": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor, School of Teacher Education",
      "description": "Western Kentucky University\nJob Posting: Academic Advisor, School of Teacher Education Western Kentucky University \n\tJob Posting: Academic Advisor, School of Teacher Education Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Academic Advisor, School of Teacher Education Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Teacher Education Locations: Bowling Green, KY Posted: Nov 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 994832 Position ID: 206630 Share About Western Kentucky University: Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience and to elevating its surrounding communities. Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293 students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors, and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville, KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents. Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . Job Description: The School of Teacher Education within the College of Education & Behavioral Sciences is pleased to announce we are accepting applications for the position of Academic Advisor. The successful candidate will serve as the initial advising point of contact for undergraduate and graduate students and be responsible for the following: Conduct student advising primarily through regular and consistent in-person and face-to-face advising sessions as required to support student success through individual and group sessions. Virtual advising sessions are also needed to accommodate graduate and non-traditional students. Work closely with Advising and Career Development to support student success, i.e., retention, persistence, and degree completion. Advise and train faculty for effective student advising and best practices, including communication of the current and new processes and policies affecting student advising. Collaborate with program area faculty and engage in effective marketing and recruitment initiatives, student success activities and other special projects as required. Attend program and department meetings as needed. This position is fully in-person/on-campus without the option for remote work as face-to-face advising is required. It is housed on the main campus of Western Kentucky University and requires daily office hours on campus for full-time employment. Occasional weekend and night activities are required. Must be available for limited travel. Other duties may be assigned for special projects or other department needs. Requirements: Bachelor's Degree Strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills Excellent organization and attention to details Ability to effectively use technology, including academic advising software and database systems Availability for limited travel, evening, and weekend work Ability to work independently and manage a large advising load in a fast-paced office environment Additional Information: Salary:  $36,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Application Instructions: The following items must be submitted through this electronic talent management system: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcript or Copy of Official Transcript Names and contact information of three reference providers will be collected during the application process. You will receive email confirmation once you have successfully completed the application process. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101"
